{"kind":"event","event_id":4449,"event_uid":"01M2K4YR3N57EW11VG8WVNJTH1","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.metadata_updated","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":214,"issue_uid":"01M2K4XHZH60EM0NHAS18290DG","issue_short_id":"90dg","actor":"impl:1@run-151","hlc_physical_ms":1789496615029,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"7d1aa467f0de33b0aaefd09bb9bbeaf92f4313a1132eb99cd5fd56725cea354e","payload":{"diff":{"work.attention":{"from":null,"to":"ok"}},"revision_new":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-15T18:23:35.029Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T18:23:35.029Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":4469,"event_uid":"01M2K516ATE35RHV406G860S77","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":214,"issue_uid":"01M2K4XHZH60EM0NHAS18290DG","issue_short_id":"90dg","actor":"impl:1@run-151","hlc_physical_ms":1789496695130,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"435a63ecf42f93a0fd381aedf5e3d58d31f10903614e1fc74b362701a64aad52","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2K516AR8W80TXF2KY7DWJFF","author":"impl:1@run-151","body":"Approach: gate foldTrigger's aged clause on `inFlight === 0 && foldingLanes === 0` — the idle half of `end` without `end`'s \"nothing ready\" — exempting `threshold === 0` so `foldAgeMs: 0` keeps BASE's fold-at-every-landing rule. With that gate the clause cannot come true while a lane sleeps, so `nextLandingOrAge` and its unref'd timer are deleted and `lane()` awaits `nextLanding()` alone. CONTRACT.md's aged sentence gains the in-flight conjunct and the `0` reading gains \"siblings in flight or not\". The exam (fleet/tests/test_run_engine_fold_policy.mjs) is peer-written and driver-laid, so I do not touch it.","created_at":"2026-09-15T18:24:55.128921699Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T18:24:55.13Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":4485,"event_uid":"01M2K56GEMWE13DM7D5QFAE89G","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":214,"issue_uid":"01M2K4XHZH60EM0NHAS18290DG","issue_short_id":"90dg","actor":"impl:1@run-151","hlc_physical_ms":1789496869332,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"617de816d222fe819de53d81b2f5538013d7c5fc69a5d37eeb366e2c6eeaf3d9","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2K56GEKXGJF7NV2CD9HNES4","author":"impl:1@run-151","body":"Landed. `foldTrigger` aged line: `const idle = threshold === 0 || (inFlight === 0 && foldingLanes === 0)` — `0` exempt so the three foldAgeMs:0 sims and the exam's b2/c2/h1 hold unedited; all three pass unedited on the patched tree. `nextLandingOrAge` deleted (no residue anywhere under fleet/), lane awaits `nextLanding()`.\n\nVerified locally with a scratch harness (written under fleet/tests/, run, deleted — not committed) reproducing the peer exam's shapes: M4/leg (e) yields exactly three adoptions ['X'] released ['Z'] / ['Y'] aged / ['Z'] end with impl:Z opening on adoption 1's headSha — so `aged` is still reachable under a positive threshold, woken by the fold release rather than a timer; M8/leg (i) positive yields one ['A','B','C'] end after C's end with no epoch event before it, and foldAgeMs:0 yields ['A'] aged before B's end; M2/leg (b)+(f) yields one ['A','B'] end with ts not before B's worker:end.\n\nExpected local red: the BASE copy of test_run_engine_fold_policy.mjs fails scenario d2, which pins the retired behaviour (A adopted ALONE why:'aged' with B open). Under the gate that run yields ['A','B'] why:'end' — exactly what M2 and leg (b) ask for. The peer's re-aimed exam replaces that file at handoff.","created_at":"2026-09-15T18:27:49.331763645Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T18:27:49.332Z"}
