{"kind":"event","event_id":4488,"event_uid":"01M2K57DSSBCY9AD0ADMAQ47NJ","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":214,"issue_uid":"01M2K4XHZH60EM0NHAS18290DG","issue_short_id":"90dg","actor":"exam:1@run-151","hlc_physical_ms":1789496899385,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"9bfea163014c3b5a63a593e818e1df96ee0c03fe8f0ee66250f0c37d0b51743a","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2K57DSRD3673M559G4THN1E","author":"exam:1@run-151","body":"exam (run-151 task 1): extending `fleet/tests/test_run_engine_fold_policy.mjs` in place, under a banner naming this task, rather than opening a second file — as the task's Context asks. Plan: re-aim BASE's `d2` (A+B, `foldAgeMs: 300`, B held 2000 ms) from \"A adopted alone, `aged`\" to M2's \"no epoch event before `worker:end impl:B`, then exactly one adoption `['A','B']` `why: 'end'`\", and retire BASE leg (e)'s WAKE_SLACK_MS window in favour of M5's negative pin (the adoption's `ts` is not before B's end). Four new runs: `c3` (the same A/B run at `foldAgeMs: 0`, M3), `e1` (X/Y/Z with X→Z, the kernel's first fold held until Y's reviewer returned plus 600 ms, M4 — the reading a positive threshold can still produce), `i1` and `i2` (A/B/C, B held 500 ms and C held 2000 ms, at 300 and at 0, M8). The leg-(a) sweep grows the aged-identity question (an `aged` adoption under a non-zero threshold is only `e1`'s) and its `RUNS.length` precondition. Leg (g) adds the third `Run:` line's fuller ordered chain to the CONTRACT.md region already read. M5's `nextLandingOrAge` pin stays with its two `Run:` lines — the task says the definition and the call, not a bare-word grep in the sim. Probing the fold's own wall first, because M8's `foldAgeMs: 0` half asks that A's adoption EVENT precede a `worker:end` 500 ms after dispatch.","created_at":"2026-09-15T18:28:19.384079430Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T18:28:19.385Z"}
