{"kind":"event","event_id":4506,"event_uid":"01M2K5VK215XY36N6Z561433TR","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":214,"issue_uid":"01M2K4XHZH60EM0NHAS18290DG","issue_short_id":"90dg","actor":"exam:1@run-151","hlc_physical_ms":1789497560129,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"2debef6ffb0d6dc1c7e0f5ce69f9737842ea6cc62723b6618e58e4efab926ffc","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2K5VK1ZSXKN1WWN7GMHZAX4","author":"exam:1@run-151","body":"exam handed in: `fleet/tests/test_run_engine_fold_policy.mjs` extended in place (475 insertions), red at BASE on leg (b) — `d2`'s run folds `['A']` `why: 'aged'` at ~630 ms with B open, where the leg asks for no epoch event at all before `worker:end impl:B`. Verified both ways: against a throwaway reference patch (the `aged` line gated on `threshold === 0 || (inFlight === 0 && foldingLanes === 0)`, `nextLandingOrAge` deleted, the lane awaiting `nextLanding()`, and the two CONTRACT.md sentences) the extended exam is green four runs running, `test_run_engine_ready_set.mjs` is green unedited, the three `Run:` greps pass, and `pytest -q -n auto tests/test_fleet_suite.py` is 28 passed — i.e. the exam is red at BASE and satisfiable by the implementation the Machine clauses describe, under parallel load. That patch was reverted; only the exam file is modified.\n\nThree readings worth keeping:\n\n1. LEG (f) IS THE TS PIN ONLY. M5 says the removal of `nextLandingOrAge` is 'pinned by M5's two `Run:` lines, the definition and the call, not the bare word', so the sim reads nothing out of `fleet/run-engine.mjs`. What it asserts is the behavioural negative: in leg (b)'s run the one adoption's `ts` is not less than `worker:end impl:B`'s. A timer-woken lane folded ~1700 ms earlier, so the pin is real without the sim knowing the function's name.\n\n2. LEG (a) ASKS IDENTITY, NOT IDLENESS. The sweep now reads each run's own `ageArgs` and asks that an `aged` adoption under a non-zero threshold belongs only to leg (e)'s run `e1`. It does NOT ask 'no worker was open before every `aged` event' — measured on `e1`, a lane woken by fold 1 dispatches Z at +1485 between the `aged` claim and its event at +1818, so that sweep would be false on a CORRECT engine. M1 is established by legs (b) and (i)'s negatives instead, as the task's Context says.\n\n3. TWO SCENARIO SHAPES ARE RACE-PROOFED DELIBERATELY. In `e1` (M4) Y waits for `worker:end impl:X` and then sleeps STAGGER_MS before writing: without the stagger Y's landing can beat X's claim by the poll interval and epoch 1 folds `['X','Y']`, which is a different run than M4's. And the margin M8's `foldAgeMs: 0` half lives on is thin by construction — A's adoption EVENT lands ~285 ms after dispatch against B's `worker:end` at ~505 ms, so the fold's own wall (kernel fold + candidate suite, ~270-350 ms here) has ~220 ms of slack. It held in the parallel bridge run; a box where one fold takes over half a second would make `i2` the first thing to go red, and that is a rig fact, not the engine's.","created_at":"2026-09-15T18:39:20.127714094Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T18:39:20.129Z"}
